-- AT-204 prerequisite — "Migration A" for event mode. Spec: docs/FAVO_PRD_v7.md
-- §6.6, §6.11, §10.2 (event_profiles, event_windows), §10.3 (opening_sessions
-- columns), §10.6 (one open session), L25–L27, REQ-042/043/044.
-- Generated by drizzle-kit from db/schema.ts + db/enums.ts, then hand-edited
-- where noted.
--
-- PROVISIONAL NUMBER: 0036. 0034 is contested by two open PRs (and 0035 is
-- left for whichever of them lands second). Renumber the file, the snapshot
-- (drizzle/meta/0036_snapshot.json), the journal tag/idx and the down script
-- if the sequence settles differently. The snapshot's prevId is 0033's.
--
--   1. enums event_menu_scope, event_payment_posture, event_audience (§6.6)
--   2. event_profiles — reusable definition, recurrence NULL = one-off
--   3. event_windows — one occurrence; six switches snapshotted at open;
--      ends_at NOT NULL; CHECK ends_at > starts_at and at most 24 h (L27)
--   4. opening_sessions: event_window_id, voucher_slips_counted (NULL = not
--      counted, L43), voucher_redemptions_recorded, voucher_kinds_active,
--      closed_at
--   5. opening_sessions_one_open: partial UNIQUE (tenant_id) WHERE
--      closed_at IS NULL (§6.11.1, COL-14). UNIQUE(session_date, opens_at)
--      from 0029 is KEPT — v7.0 does not narrow it.
--
-- Touches no payments, orders or order_items object.
--
-- Hand edits: (a) this header; (b) before the index, sessions from a past
-- revenue day get closed_at = the next SAST midnight (L07: a session never
-- straddles midnight; closeSession is forced at the day boundary). Zero rows
-- on a clean database (PRD §13.0); (c) a guard that refuses, and changes
-- nothing, if more than one of today's sessions would still be open.
-- The reverse is drizzle/down/0036_at204_event_sessions.down.sql.

